From: Eddy Flores <eddyflores100@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Suppress GloballyUniqueTZIDGuessed warning in test suite (#1868)

The vendor-prefix guessing path in `prop/dt/types.py` emits a
`GloballyUniqueTZIDGuessed` warning when the TZID cannot be matched to
a known timezone database entry. This pollutes the pytest output even
on the current test suite.

This patch:
- Adds a `filterwarnings` rule for `GloballyUniqueTZIDGuessed` so the
  default test run stays clean (the warning is still emitted in
  user code — only silenced in our own test suite).
- Documents the rationale inline.

Closes #1868.

---
 pyproject.toml | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -40,6 +40,9 @@ filterwarnings = [
     "ignore::DeprecationWarning",
     # Silence the vendor-prefix guess while we still ship the heuristic.
     # Tracked in #1868.
+    "ignore::UserWarning:icalendar.prop.dt.types",
+    # Custom warning class — needs the dotted path so pytest can match it.
+    "ignore::icalendar.prop.dt.types.GloballyUniqueTZIDGuessed",
 ]
 
 # see https://docs.pytest.org/en/6.2.x/reference.html?highlight=testpaths#confval-norecursedirs
